# 4. Replace `processFile()` with seek-based processing

Keep the existing Spring component, health indicator, counters, fail-stop behavior, and transactional recovery.

Replace its `processFile()` method and add the helpers below.

Additional imports:

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.nio.ByteBuffer;
import java.nio.channels.Channels;
import java.nio.channels.FileChannel;
import java.nio.charset.CodingErrorAction;
import java.nio.file.StandardOpenOption;
import java.nio.file.attribute.BasicFileAttributes;
import java.util.HashSet;
```

### Replacement method

```java
private void processFile(
        Path file,
        Checkpoint previous
) throws Exception {

    String fileName = file.getFileName().toString();

    BasicFileAttributes attributes = Files.readAttributes(
            file,
            BasicFileAttributes.class,
            LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS
    );

    if (!attributes.isRegularFile()) {
        throw new IOException("Not a regular file: " + file);
    }

    long fileSize = attributes.size();
    long modifiedMillis = attributes.lastModifiedTime().toMillis();

    if (previous != null) {
        if (previous.fileSize() != fileSize
                || previous.lastModifiedMillis() != modifiedMillis) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                    "Previously checkpointed file changed: " + fileName
            );
        }
    }

    long nextRecord = previous == null ? 0 : previous.nextRecord();

    String fileId = config.sourceId() + ":" +
            Base64.getUrlEncoder()
                    .withoutPadding()
                    .encodeToString(
                            fileName.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)
                    );

    try (FileChannel channel = FileChannel.open(
            file, StandardOpenOption.READ)) {

        // For a new file, exclude an optional UTF-8 BOM from parser input.
        // For a resumed file, jump directly to the next CSV record.
        long baseOffset = previous == null
                ? utf8BomLength(channel)
                : previous.nextByteOffset();

        channel.position(baseOffset);

        CSVFormat format = previous == null
                ? CSV_FORMAT
                : CSV_FORMAT.builder()
                        .setHeader(previous.headers().toArray(String[]::new))
                        .setSkipHeaderRecord(false)
                        .get();

        var decoder = StandardCharsets.UTF_8.newDecoder()
                .onMalformedInput(CodingErrorAction.REPORT)
                .onUnmappableCharacter(CodingErrorAction.REPORT);

        try (var reader = new BufferedReader(
                    new InputStreamReader(
                            Channels.newInputStream(channel),
                            decoder
                    ),
                    256 * 1024
             );
             CSVParser parser = CSVParser.builder()
                    .setReader(reader)
                    .setCharset(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)
                    .setFormat(format)
                    .setTrackBytes(true)
                    .get()) {

            List<String> headers = List.copyOf(parser.getHeaderNames());

            if (headers.isEmpty()
                    || headers.stream().anyMatch(String::isBlank)
                    || new HashSet<>(headers).size() != headers.size()) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Invalid CSV headers: " + fileName
                );
            }

            var iterator = parser.iterator();

            // One-record lookahead:
            // pending is always the next record NOT in the current batch.
            CSVRecord pending = iterator.hasNext()
                    ? iterator.next()
                    : null;

            while (!stopping) {
                List<OutgoingRecord> batch = new ArrayList<>(
                        Math.min(config.batchRows(), 4096)
                );

                long batchBytes = 0;
                long started = System.nanoTime();

                while (pending != null
                        && batch.size() < config.batchRows()
                        && batchBytes < config.batchBytes()
                        && (batch.isEmpty()
                            || System.nanoTime() - started
                                < config.batchMaxAge().toNanos())) {

                    if (stopping) {
                        return;
                    }

                    CSVRecord csv = pending;

                    if (!csv.isConsistent()) {
                        throw new IllegalStateException(
                                "Column count mismatch: file=" + fileName
                                + ", record=" + nextRecord
                        );
                    }

                    Map<String, String> data = new LinkedHashMap<>();

                    for (int column = 0; column < headers.size(); column++) {
                        data.put(headers.get(column), csv.get(column));
                    }

                    String eventId = fileId + ":" + nextRecord;

                    Map<String, Object> event = new LinkedHashMap<>();
                    event.put("schemaVersion", 2);
                    event.put("eventId", eventId);
                    event.put("sourceId", config.sourceId());
                    event.put("fileName", fileName);
                    event.put("recordIndex", nextRecord);
                    event.put("data", data);

                    byte[] payload = json.writeValueAsBytes(event);

                    if (payload.length > config.maxRecordBytes()) {
                        throw new IllegalStateException(
                                "Event exceeds configured size limit: file="
                                + fileName + ", record=" + nextRecord
                        );
                    }

                    batch.add(new OutgoingRecord(eventId, payload));
                    batchBytes += payload.length;
                    nextRecord++;

                    pending = iterator.hasNext()
                            ? iterator.next()
                            : null;
                }

                boolean completed = pending == null;

                // getBytePosition() is relative to this parser's input.
                // Add the file position at which that parser was opened.
                long nextByteOffset = completed
                        ? fileSize
                        : Math.addExact(
                                baseOffset,
                                pending.getBytePosition()
                        );

                if (nextByteOffset < baseOffset
                        || nextByteOffset > fileSize) {
                    throw new IllegalStateException(
                            "Invalid parser byte offset: " + fileName
                    );
                }

                if (stopping) {
                    return;
                }

                assertUnchanged(file, fileSize, modifiedMillis);

                Checkpoint checkpoint = new Checkpoint(
                        2,
                        config.sourceId(),
                        fileName,
                        fileSize,
                        modifiedMillis,
                        headers,
                        nextRecord,
                        nextByteOffset,
                        completed
                );

                // Same atomicity as before:
                // output records + checkpoint in ONE transaction.
                journal.commit(batch, checkpoint);

                committedRecords.increment(batch.size());
                committedTransactions.increment();

                // Avoid an INFO log for every batch at high throughput.
                log.debug(
                        "Committed file={} rows={} nextRecord={} "
                        + "nextByteOffset={} completed={}",
                        fileName,
                        batch.size(),
                        nextRecord,
                        nextByteOffset,
                        completed
                );

                if (completed) {
                    log.info(
                            "Completed file={} records={} bytes={}",
                            fileName,
                            nextRecord,
                            fileSize
                    );
                    return;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Helpers

```java
private static long utf8BomLength(FileChannel channel) throws IOException {
    ByteBuffer bytes = ByteBuffer.allocate(3);

    // Positional reads do not change the channel's current position.
    while (bytes.hasRemaining()) {
        int count = channel.read(bytes, bytes.position());

        if (count < 0) {
            break;
        }

        if (count == 0) {
            throw new IOException("Could not read file prefix");
        }
    }

    return bytes.position() == 3
            && (bytes.get(0) & 0xff) == 0xef
            && (bytes.get(1) & 0xff) == 0xbb
            && (bytes.get(2) & 0xff) == 0xbf
            ? 3
            : 0;
}

private static void assertUnchanged(
        Path file,
        long expectedSize,
        long expectedModifiedMillis
) throws IOException {

    BasicFileAttributes attributes = Files.readAttributes(
            file,
            BasicFileAttributes.class,
            LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS
    );

    if (!attributes.isRegularFile()
            || attributes.size() != expectedSize
            || attributes.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()
                != expectedModifiedMillis) {
        throw new IOException(
                "Published file changed during processing: " + file
        );
    }
}
```

### Why the lookahead matters

Suppose a batch contains records `0–999`.

The parser has also read record `1000` into `pending`, but that record is **not published yet**.

The transaction saves:

```text
nextRecord     = 1000
nextByteOffset = start of record 1000
```

If the process crashes, it seeks to record `1000`, not to wherever the buffered file channel happened to stop.

This also accommodates quoted multiline fields and UTF-8 text. The relevant Commons CSV APIs track the record start separately from the underlying reader’s buffered position. ([commons.apache.org](https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-csv/apidocs/org/apache/commons/csv/CSVRecord.html?utm_source=openai))

**Performance caveat:** byte tracking itself adds CPU work; the pinned Commons CSV implementation calculates encoded character lengths. Benchmark steady-state parsing throughput as well as restart time rather than assuming byte tracking makes parsing faster. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/apache/commons-csv/rel/commons-csv-1.14.1/src/main/java/org/apache/commons/csv/ExtendedBufferedReader.java))

