### Replace `commit()`

```java
public void commit(
        List<OutgoingRecord> records,
        Checkpoint checkpoint
) {
    byte[] checkpointBytes = json.writeValueAsBytes(checkpoint);

    producer.beginTransaction();

    for (OutgoingRecord record : records) {
        producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>(
                config.outputTopic(),
                record.key(),
                record.payload()
        ));
    }

    producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>(
            config.checkpointTopic(),
            0,
            FILE_PREFIX + checkpoint.fileName(),
            checkpointBytes
    ));

    producer.commitTransaction();

    remember(checkpoint);
}
```

Do not add `.get()` after every `send()`. The sends should remain asynchronous; transaction commit waits for outstanding sends and handles their failures. ([kafka.apache.org](https://kafka.apache.org/41/javadoc/org/apache/kafka/clients/producer/KafkaProducer.html))

